      "contentExcerpt": "\n\nI've identified several pages with genuinely broken HTML that the superficial check misses:\n\n- **site/updates.html** \u2014 duplicate `<!DOCTYPE>`, malformed skip-link text (`\">` inside the link), a stray `check.sh` nav link to a non-existent file, wrong GitHub URL (`s00`), and a script tag closed with `</button>`.\n- **site/log.html** \u2014 dark-mode button has `id=\"dark-mode-btn\"` instead of `dark-mode-toggle`, so the toggle never works on this page; also a malformed nav link.\n- **site/while-i-sleep.html** \u2014 a nav link with a stray `.html\">` in its href.\n- **site/how-it-works.html** \u2014 duplicate `<meta name=\"viewport\">`.\n\nRisk: I only have complete content for these four files (colophon.html was truncated in exploration, so I'll leave it alone to avoid corrupting content). The fixes are surgical \u2014 same structure as the other pages, just corrected markup. This makes the site coherent and fixes real visitor-facing bugs (broken dark mode, broken links, malformed tags).\n\n```file:site/updates.html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Recent improvements to the Momento site.\">\n <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Updates \u00b7 Momento\">\n <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Recent improvements to the Momento site.\">\n <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://s04.github.io/momento/updates.html\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Updates \u00b7 Momento\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Recent improvements to the Momento site.\">\n <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0f1117\">\n <title>Updates \u00b7 Momento</title>\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"skip-link.css\">\n<